{% comment %}
  Animated stand-ins for two product gallery images, swapped in by product-thumbnail
  (gallery) and product-media (zoom view):
  - 'chart': "Why people are switching to Vura" (replaces vura_benefits_2). Five of the
    nine rows of the original chart, claims unchanged, led by the two only Vura wins.
  - 'benefits': the six benefits around the bottle (replaces vura_benefits_1), without the
    image generator's "*Only include claims..." line that is printed on the original.

  The markup is the finished slide, so it reads complete without script, with reduced
  motion, and in the zoom view. vura-proof-slides-assets hides the marks and draws them in
  when the slide comes into view.

  Generated from a script (fixed hand-drawn jitter); edit the text here freely, but keep
  the vp-d / vp-wash classes and their --d (delay) / --t (duration) styles.

  Accepts:
  - kind: {String} 'chart' or 'benefits'
  - alt: {String} text alternative, the original image's alt
  - animate: {Boolean} draw in when it scrolls into view (false in the zoom view)
{% endcomment %}
<div class="vura-proof vura-proof--{{ kind }}"{% if animate %} data-vura-proof{% endif %} role="img" aria-label="{{ alt | escape }}">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 400 400" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    {%- if kind == 'chart' -%}
      <rect width="400" height="400" fill="#F4EFE3"/>
      <text x="18" y="52" class="vp-title">Why people are</text>
      <text x="18" y="83" class="vp-title">switching to <tspan fill="#8D3B2D">Vura</tspan></text>
